{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1170678-advice-on-a-plothook","id":1170678,"title":"Advice on a plothook","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-26T08:12:32-08:00","id":1170678,"title":"Advice on a plothook","content":"I just got C:20 yesterday and while thinking about plothooks, I got an interesting idea I want advice on. This plothook focuses on the PCs meeting a accountant named Howard Conners, a mousy gentleman who works for Pericles Land Development Corporation. Howard, ever since he was a child, had always had a fantasy about becoming a Superhero, this fantasy was especially there after he was mugged outside of his workplace. The strange part is that something or someone ends up granting Howard's fantasy after he somehow manages to fight off street thugs with new-found strength.<br /> <br /> The plot would have the PC's try to figure out who or what granted Howard's fantasy while making sure he doesn't kill himself, especially after he ends up pissing off his own employer, who had recently took a contract with The Bellerophon Institute to build a new facility in the area. How could this plothook work in Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T13:43:55-08:00","id":1170759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1170678-advice-on-a-plothook#post1170678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got C:20 yesterday and while thinking about plothooks, I got an interesting idea I want advice on. This plothook focuses on the PCs meeting a accountant named Howard Conners, a mousy gentleman who works for Pericles Land Development Corporation. Howard, ever since he was a child, had always had a fantasy about becoming a Superhero, this fantasy was especially there after he was mugged outside of his workplace. The strange part is that something or someone ends up granting Howard's fantasy after he somehow manages to fight off street thugs with new-found strength.<br /> <br /> The plot would have the PC's try to figure out who or what granted Howard's fantasy while making sure he doesn't kill himself, especially after he ends up pissing off his own employer, who had recently took a contract with The Bellerophon Institute to build a new facility in the area. How could this plothook work in Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I too, just got the book yesterday, congratulations!<br /> <br /> As for how the plot hook might work, I'm not too sure (mostly because I haven't been able to read through the whole book, yet). But Dreaming is a game about exploring the limitless possibilities of imagination, so there's any number of ways this could go about happening.<br /> <br /> <br /> The wannabe super hero might have just gone through their chrysalis without even realizing it. The book says once the fae spirit merges with you, you feel as if you were always meant to be that way.<br /> <br /> Another is that they've somehow become enchanted. I don't know if enchanted mortals get any kind of powers, so that might require some more reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T23:27:36-08:00","id":1170870,"title":"","content":"In my game I've had a similar situation appear, a small group of mundanes begin to show abilities that exceed the normal restraints of reality. The First of Three ended up having a Treasure buried deep in his dreamrealm, the magic within beginning to bubble out and affect the Dreamer. They began to seek out Unseelie Changelings and fight these 'Villains!', the resulting enchanted 'superhero' began to collect chimerical items in the process, and making chimerical companions to serve as minions. He's beginning to manifest the ability to invoke the wyrd and once that happens who knows what this mad dreamer will be capable of!<br /> <br /> The players dont know who would leave a potent unstable treasure hidden in a old dreamers dreamscape, the Hero claims the Tree/Treasure was planted by the Gardener of Dreams, and all thoughts thus far are to a being from the Deep Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}